#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df6ae15d-7005-5a93-9432-c4814dc9573d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Terms in an Arithmetic Series Given the Pattern and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34539436-5aab-593a-9db3-570b029285b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341814} {:answer/id #uuid "4281a1aa-8a8d-520b-858f-83ce096896ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341815} {:answer/id #uuid "5281f2cf-1988-5c30-950a-61f4575006f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341816} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ecc6f9-9ab6-566b-a4f0-4642ebf61ed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341817} {:answer/id #uuid "c317bd27-9f07-5931-b443-7cfbc1ed0ca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5281f2cf-1988-5c30-950a-61f4575006f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341816} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9dd24f7-26b9-5c21-b7c9-92d0a30568ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "909f6f75-e3ee-52dd-8226-a8816ba53faa" :question/math-academy-id "q-108909" :question/problem "Calculate the number of terms in the following arithmetic series. \n\n$$\n4.2+4.7+5.2+...=139.4\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nWe have been given the sum ${S}_{N}=139.4,$ and the first term ${a}_{1}=4.2.$ Our goal is to find $N,$ the number of terms.\n\nThe common difference $d$ can be found, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =4.7-4.2 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 139.4 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(4.2)+(N-1)(0.5)) \\\\ 278.8 & =N(8.4+0.5N-0.5) \\\\ 278.8 & =N(7.9+0.5N) \\\\ 278.8 & =7.9N+0.5{N}^{2} \\\\ 0.5{N}^{2}+7.9N-278.8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-7.9\\pm \\sqrt{(-7.9)^{2}-4\\cdot 0.5\\cdot (-278.8)}}{2\\cdot 0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7.9\\pm 24.9}{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $N=17$ or $N=-32.8.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive and integer.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=17$ terms."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b23f178-4161-56d3-98e0-00b3181417e2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Terms in an Arithmetic Series Given Two Terms and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a423087-06fa-51ac-b7d4-dcc7ce50509d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341821} {:answer/id #uuid "899fec80-d87c-52ee-9fd3-008e266e2bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341822} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb94118-de2b-5718-adcb-42123b7bc9e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341823} {:answer/id #uuid "34443807-4615-5704-9666-60f4359a45c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341824} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd8ca9d-cf1e-559b-8ec3-68ea08a61f1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbd8ca9d-cf1e-559b-8ec3-68ea08a61f1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341825} :answer-field/id #uuid "c57e75b1-1ea8-5c5d-ac0f-595a4f50c885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b66f3a11-061d-54d6-aa08-eb07da948258" :question/math-academy-id "q-108939" :question/problem "An arithmetic series has the $6$th term ${a}_{6}=17,$ the $9$th term ${a}_{9}=26,$ and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=77.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{9}-{a}_{6}}{9-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{26-17}{9-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{3} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that ${a}_{6}=17.$ We can compute ${a}_{1}$ using the formula for the $n$th term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ 17 & ={a}_{1}+(6-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\ 17 & ={a}_{1}+15 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=2,$ $d=3,$ and ${S}_{N}=77$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 77 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 2+(N-1)\\cdot 3) \\\\ 154 & =N(4+3N-3) \\\\ 154 & =N(3N+1) \\\\ 154 & =3{N}^{2}+N \\\\ 3{N}^{2}+N-154 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-1\\pm \\sqrt{(1)^{2}-4\\cdot 3\\cdot (-154)}}{2\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1\\pm \\sqrt{1\\,849}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1\\pm 43}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $N=7$ or $N=-\\frac{22}{3}.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=7$ terms."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b23f178-4161-56d3-98e0-00b3181417e2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Terms in an Arithmetic Series Given Two Terms and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9240e06a-7d70-5248-8811-05ff05fbd9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341828} {:answer/id #uuid "731babb2-0850-514b-ad98-3b1da9e6034c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341829} {:answer/id #uuid "20aaa73f-6759-559c-9a8d-0f0bd74dc9ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341830} {:answer/id #uuid "900fa49a-d49a-5a1f-832e-33ea24132a2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341831} {:answer/id #uuid "71ca66f0-e607-5f92-8045-ba8308c40e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "731babb2-0850-514b-ad98-3b1da9e6034c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341829} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4cbdafe-2409-5673-ab98-4b1092a825ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c50105a1-f29d-5e55-bf71-2b6a09cdcb38" :question/math-academy-id "q-5493" :question/problem "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=5$, the second term is ${a}_{2}=15$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=845.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know the first two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =15-5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=5$, $d=10$, and ${S}_{N}=845$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 845 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(5)+(N-1)(10)) \\\\ 845 & =\\frac{N}{2}(10+10N-10) \\\\ 845 & =\\frac{N}{2}(10N) \\\\ 845 & =5{N}^{2} \\\\ 169 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df6ae15d-7005-5a93-9432-c4814dc9573d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Terms in an Arithmetic Series Given the Pattern and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "094367b1-2070-5358-8446-1ccb70845da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341835} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4c240c-0e79-57e5-8437-8e60f48c22b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341836} {:answer/id #uuid "4387757a-7093-57f4-a9eb-76699aef7484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341837} {:answer/id #uuid "c4cdcee2-5c75-5ae2-a5a9-e444ff7b2e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341838} {:answer/id #uuid "53d9bc4b-e8b3-5527-b7ee-c5c39c5e5d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "094367b1-2070-5358-8446-1ccb70845da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341835} :answer-field/id #uuid "c37d32f0-08bd-5736-9323-4538674e2b0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6459e27b-fba3-5e45-b1d1-30caddf62eb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-67070" :question/problem "Calculate the number of terms in the following arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n1+3+5+…=81\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\\,\\,\n$$\n\nWe have been given the sum ${S}_{N}=81$, and the first term ${a}_{1}=1.$ Our goal is to find $N,$ the number of terms.\n\nThe common difference $d$ can be found, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =3-1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 81 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 1+(N-1)\\cdot 2) \\\\ 81 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2+2N-2) \\\\ 81 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2N) \\\\ 81 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$can't be negative. Therefore, our series has $N=9$ terms."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df6ae15d-7005-5a93-9432-c4814dc9573d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Terms in an Arithmetic Series Given the Pattern and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94af839c-6e9c-5e9a-9fc3-be58cb065832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341842} {:answer/id #uuid "01f93ddd-9136-5415-a307-77e5be9973ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341843} {:answer/id #uuid "32824719-955c-5f65-8c6b-f13723ff0ebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341844} {:answer/id #uuid "281ddbc6-1dd6-58ff-8768-3df3d6417cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341845} {:answer/id #uuid "c32c9d1f-5b11-5080-90b2-9b33a3837bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c32c9d1f-5b11-5080-90b2-9b33a3837bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341846} :answer-field/id #uuid "9befe208-6f28-5ced-b85e-777ba50eaf7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7030e287-f48c-5532-8e39-1dfbac2979ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-67074" :question/problem "Calculate the number of terms in the following arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n5+15+25+…=180\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\\,\\,\n$$\n\nWe have been given the sum ${S}_{N}=180$, and the first term ${a}_{1}=5.$ Our goal is to find $N,$ the number of terms.\n\nThe common difference $d$ can be found, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =15-5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 180 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 5+(N-1)\\cdot 10) \\\\ 180 & =\\frac{N}{2}(10+10N-10) \\\\ 180 & =\\frac{N}{2}(10N) \\\\ 180 & =5{N}^{2} \\\\ 36 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$can't be negative. Therefore, our series has $N=6$ terms."}]}
